    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "MXd8Y",
      "x": 4755,
      "y": 15444,
      "name": "DIG · how it plays",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light",
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "clip": true,
      "width": 880,
      "fill": "$ds-sky-bottom",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kQlAW",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HOW DIG PLAYS",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LckDq",
          "name": "The bar · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The bar",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ip0gV",
          "name": "The bar · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HOME and the title on the left; on the right the ⭐ DUG UP count, the brush picker (two dot buttons, the picked one amber) and the 📖 FIELD GUIDE with its count. The title sits beside HOME, not centred, so WHO IS IT?, FIELD GUIDE and the Russian titles fit. On a phone upright the bar keeps only HOME, the title and the FIELD GUIDE; DUG UP leaves it, and both brushes stand as a pair of wide buttons at the bottom of the sand, under the thumb, each a dot with its words, the picked one amber. HOME and BACK become 48 px round symbols.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "gZNQk",
          "name": "The board · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T8Sthq",
          "name": "The board · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board is the picture's 4:3, sunk into the sand as a pocket with an inner shadow. Hatchling has no column, so its board is centred and as large as fits. Explorer and Paleontologist hold a smaller board on the left from the round's start, so nothing moves when the question comes.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t2Eusb",
          "name": "The question · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The question",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QTUIR",
          "name": "The question · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The column starts as empty ? cards and the dinosaur cards fade in over them, grey until a pick. A wrong pick fades its picture and shows TRY ANOTHER; the right one turns to colour with a green ring and ✓, then the gust. On a phone upright the cards go two to a row under the board, twice as wide as tall, picture over name; on its side they stack to the right of the board.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bpDYR",
          "name": "Finds · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Finds",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bHtjG",
          "name": "Finds · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A treasure glows where it lies, hops and flies to the FIELD GUIDE, which shows NEW! under its button the first time. A found help spot shines with an amber ring and a small star.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bkeZo",
          "name": "The reveal · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The reveal",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "l5yoLI",
          "name": "The reveal · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The game shell's result: the dinosaur in the celebration, its name large, the DUG UP card (⭐, count, NEW!, 🏆 at 52/52, 🦴 for a first-pick name), NEW BEST, the level switch, DIG AGAIN and HOME. The FIELD GUIDE stays reachable at the top right.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "fTPB9",
          "name": "FIELD GUIDE · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "FIELD GUIDE",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hJ3Nk",
          "name": "FIELD GUIDE · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Five cards in their fixed order; found ones show the picture, name and ×count, the rest an outline and ?. On an upright phone they become rows, and the title is the book alone. The upright iPad puts them in rows of two that share the height, the last one centred, with BACK and HOME as symbols in the bar. On a phone on its side the bar is short (HOME and BACK as squares, the title, FOUND) and the cards share the height: one row in English, three over two in Russian, where each card is small and upright so ЗОЛОТАЯ ОКАМЕНЕЛОСТЬ stays whole.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KWTCn",
          "name": "Motion · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Motion",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rzowO",
          "name": "Motion · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Brushing lifts small puffs of sand under the finger and the picture shows through. Each dinosaur card fades in over its ? card; the right pick turns to colour and a gust blows the last sand off the board. A treasure hops, then flies into the FIELD GUIDE; a help spot's ring shines once. The reveal's dinosaur rises with the celebration and NEW BEST pops. Every change uses the shared quick motion; reduced motion turns each into a short fade and the gust into a quick clear.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Ow9YD",
          "name": "Every device · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Every device",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Gj6Y4",
          "name": "Every device · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Phones and the upright iPad stack the board over the dinosaur cards, with BRUSH and WIDE BRUSH as one wide bar at the bottom of the sand; the upright bar holds HOME, the title and the FIELD GUIDE, and the DUG UP count waits for the reveal. On a phone on its side the board and cards sit side by side and the whole bar fits in one row; the reveal puts the dinosaur on the left, the name and score on the right, and the level switch and buttons in one row on the sand. On iPhone SE the reveal's two buttons stack and its rows shrink to fit 667 without scrolling. In Russian a long button word breaks onto two lines (ШИРОКАЯ / КИСТЬ) rather than shrinking.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GB2yQ",
          "name": "Dark · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Dark",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "klxWD",
          "name": "Dark · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board keeps the picture's own light sand: it is the dinosaur's picture, not a surface, so it reads as a lit pit in the dark ground.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
