    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "dyySG",
      "x": 7400,
      "y": 27100,
      "name": "PAIRS · levels · how it plays",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light",
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "clip": true,
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$ds-sky-bottom",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "foNcH",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HOW FIND THE PAIR PLAYS AT EACH LEVEL",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "c7czbh",
          "name": "Welcome · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Welcome",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "o1vkP",
          "name": "Welcome · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The game mark, the title, three hero cards (face down, silhouette, picture) and the boards and stars chips. The level switch sits above PLAY; on phones the chosen level alone shows its name, the others show only their pictures. The first visit shows boards 0 and no best.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "oQtrx",
          "name": "Cards · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Cards",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "OkyFZ",
          "name": "Cards · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A face-down card is ink with footprints. Pressed it turns orange and shrinks a little. Turned over it shows a picture, a silhouette or a skeleton on cream. A found pair gets a green outline and its name. Loading shows a shimmer; a picture that fails shows the name large instead.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "u6bIPA",
          "name": "Hatchling · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Hatchling",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bjsqj",
          "name": "Hatchling · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Pictures only, and the only level that climbs: level 1 has 3 pairs, then 4, 5 and 6. Two finished boards move up a level; level 4 keeps going. The bar shows the climb level and the tries.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dSz7A",
          "name": "Explorer · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Explorer",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "G6hLY",
          "name": "Explorer · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "9 pairs in 3 rows of 6; each pair is a dinosaur's picture and its silhouette. No two dinosaurs of a board come from the same look-alike group.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ODGCO",
          "name": "Paleontologist · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Paleontologist",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nVwHw",
          "name": "Paleontologist · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "12 pairs in 4 rows of 6; each pair is a picture and the whole skeleton, drawn in its own bone colour. Only dinosaurs with a whole skeleton are dealt.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "EJfJ4",
          "name": "Result · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Result",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "n5X5T",
          "name": "Result · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board's dinosaurs, new finds marked NEW; the tries beside a hand; a star that flies into the stars count; WELL DONE!; and the best: first best and new best in yellow, a kept best quiet with its trophy. Hatchling's level-up shows NEW LEVEL with a small map of the next board. PLAY AGAIN deals the same level, BACK returns to the welcome, HOME goes home.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GYJm3",
          "name": "Level offer · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Level offer",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "U2l4JS",
          "name": "Level offer · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Three strong boards in a row (at most twice the pairs in tries) offer the next level: climb 4 Hatchling boards offer Explorer, Explorer boards offer Paleontologist. It rises over the result after the star and the best, with NOT NOW and YES; the result's buttons wait under the scrim.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kPEQS",
          "name": "Names on small cards · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Names on small cards",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "x58FI3",
          "name": "Names on small cards · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "On phones the board's cards show no names; the result names every dinosaur. A name over 15 letters is drawn smaller; where it would fall under 9 pt it breaks at its hyphen point onto two lines (TYRANNO-/SAURUS, ТИРАННО-/ЗАВР), never under 7 pt.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PsvPI",
          "name": "Motion · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Motion",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "U7jOe",
          "name": "Motion · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A card flips over its vertical axis; a found pair bounces once; a miss waits, then both flip back. When the last pair is found every card does a short happy wave. The result's star flies into the count; the offer rises over a scrim. Reduced motion turns each into a short fade.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RnehC",
          "name": "Every device, dark and Russian · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Every device, dark and Russian",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ZxeQh",
          "name": "Every device, dark and Russian · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Boards, welcomes and results are drawn for the iPad mini on its side and upright, the iPhone, the iPhone SE and the iPhone on its side, with dark and Russian versions. Dark mode swaps silhouettes for their cream versions.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "O1NPjA",
          "name": "Art to fix · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Art to fix",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "X8W93S",
          "name": "Art to fix · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Skeleton bones average about 2.8:1 against the cream card, under 3:1: the skeleton art needs a darker outline. Velociraptor, compsognathus, gallimimus and therizinosaurus have no silhouette yet; until they do, Explorer cannot deal them.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "GdXub",
      "x": 9300,
      "y": 2050,
      "name": "Components · SORT · Light",
