    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "SfDL7",
      "x": 9900,
      "y": 53800,
      "name": "BONES · how it plays",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light",
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "clip": true,
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$ds-sky-bottom",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xuShQ",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HOW BONES PLAYS",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DTvob",
          "name": "Levels · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Levels",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xz4ni",
          "name": "Levels · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The level switch (🥚 HATCHLING, 🦖 EXPLORER, 🦴 PALEONTOLOGIST) sits above the dinosaurs, the same switch PAIRS uses. Hatchling builds four straight-cut pieces, Explorer six to eight bones by body area, Paleontologist up to ten with other dinosaurs' bones mixed into the tray. The child's choice is kept until a parent changes the age level.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dGQd3",
          "name": "Choice · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Choice",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "wv33u",
          "name": "Choice · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Five skeleton cards, each a body picture, with the earned star in its corner. The best chip counts skeletons finished. Once one star is earned, a \"?\" mystery tile ends the list.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "FJerO",
          "name": "Board and tray · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Board and tray",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "gMTaD",
          "name": "Board and tray · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board keeps the outline frame's shape, as large as fits beside the tray (landscape) or above it (portrait). The outline is a faint skeleton, or at Paleontologist a flat silhouette in the theme's own colour. Tray spots are square, at least 48 px, in as many columns as they need. A fitted bone leaves its spot empty. The counter reads fitted / total.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "EmyAm",
          "name": "A held bone · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A held bone",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "aaiTm",
          "name": "A held bone · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The bone lifts with a soft shadow at the size it fits on the board. Only Hatchling outlines its home while it is held. A drop beside the board wobbles back with a \"boing\"; nothing is lost.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "M6NQ6",
          "name": "Help · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Help",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "IRYQV",
          "name": "Help · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "No failure, no timer on screen. Hatchling: after 10 s with no bone fitted, one slot and its spot glow. Explorer and Paleontologist climb a ladder for the first unfitted bone: at 10 s its body region and spot glow, at 20 s a faint ghost shows at its home, at 30 s the bone moves part way home and back once (a fade under reduced motion). A fitted bone clears help and starts again; a touch pauses it.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "gxV2K",
          "name": "Another dinosaur's bone · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Another dinosaur's bone",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "l9bQea",
          "name": "Another dinosaur's bone · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Paleontologist only. Dropped on the outline, it floats back to its spot with a \"boing\" and a line names it: \"THAT'S THE TRICERATOPS FRILL!\" The line goes the moment another bone is touched.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "L2aeBl",
          "name": "Complete · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Complete",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "g5VzMU",
          "name": "Complete · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The last bone fitted: the counter turns green, the skeleton stomps twice and its jaw snaps with a roar, then the body fades in over it. Reduced motion keeps the sounds and stills the movement.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V8FG1z",
          "name": "Result · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Result",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iODSH",
          "name": "Result · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Body over skeleton, name, one short fact with a bulb. A new star pops with a NEW tag; a first or new best gets its celebration chip; a level badge is earned when the last help step never showed (none at Hatchling). A rebuild keeps the star and shows the best kept. BUILD ANOTHER and MUSEUM.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j8noL",
          "name": "Museum · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Museum",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VtX6S",
          "name": "Museum · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Five stands, three above and two centred below, on no cards: built (skeleton, star, badges, REBUILD), awaiting rebuild (faint silhouette in an amber ring, CONTINUE), empty (silhouette, BUILD), plus the jaw shelf. Each button stands on its own.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "p5lbQ",
          "name": "Mystery and guess · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Mystery and guess",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DlIhC",
          "name": "Mystery and guess · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The \"?\" builds an already starred skeleton with its name hidden. Complete, it asks WHOSE SKELETON IS IT? with three bodies. A wrong one wobbles, rests aside faded and can't be tapped, and the line gives a clue. The right one reveals as usual, with no new star.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ctlLs",
          "name": "Pictures · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Pictures",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "YBt2J",
          "name": "Pictures · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A puzzle starts at once: the outline and bones shimmer and each picture fades in (200 ms) when loaded. A picture that fails shows a quiet bone mark; the bone still fits. Result and museum shimmer the same way and never wait for a picture.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ViU6J",
          "name": "Phones · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Phones",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GwVit",
          "name": "Phones · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Portrait puts the tray under the board and the result's reward in the sand; the iPhone SE tightens the reveal. On its side the title moves into the bar and the tray sits beside the board.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "vfkNP",
          "name": "Motion · head",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Motion",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V0kCE",
          "name": "Motion · body",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Shared motion tokens: bones snap home with a little bounce, the tray reflows, the star pops, the celebration bursts, stands rise in. Reduced motion uses short fades.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
