    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "F04B2",
      "x": 11200,
      "y": 71800,
      "name": "PUZZLE · how it plays",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light",
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$ds-sky-bottom",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s2MTlr",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "PUZZLE · how it plays",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HI5Zc",
          "name": "Head · Every device plays",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Every device plays",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dAfb9",
          "name": "Body · Every device plays",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Landscape iPad: tray beside the board. Upright iPad and phones: tray under the board, four pieces in a row. Phone on its side: a 2×2 tray with round tools. Board widths are multiples of 48, so the 4×3, 6×4 and 6×6 cuts give whole-pixel tiles that meet with no seams.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AEgGU",
          "name": "Head · Levels",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Levels",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VDNKR",
          "name": "Body · Levels",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Hatchling is the current 4×3 game, with a faint guide of the whole picture under the empty slots. Explorer is 6×4, Paleontologist 6×6. The choice shows the three dinosaur scenes, the level switch and a star on each dinosaur in the shared collection.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XNO7W",
          "name": "Head · Turn gate",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Turn gate",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cnupz",
          "name": "Body · Turn gate",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Paleontologist on an upright phone would give 45-point tiles, too small for young fingers, so TURN SIDEWAYS covers the board, which waits behind it and keeps its pieces. The parent note is small and faded. Hatchling and Explorer play upright everywhere; the app's current gate covers every upright screen, and this design narrows it to that one case.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hiwYZ",
          "name": "Head · Placing pieces",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Placing pieces",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "FXxiL",
          "name": "Body · Placing pieces",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Drag a piece from the tray onto the board, or tap it (terracotta ring) and tap a slot. A fitting piece snaps in and the counter ticks up. A wrong drop glides back to its spot with a wobble and TRY AGAIN; nothing is lost. Keyboard: arrows move a navy focus ring over the slots and Enter places the selected piece. The tray shows four pieces a page.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KMuJf",
          "name": "Head · Help",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Help",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j27VO",
          "name": "Body · Help",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HINT turns amber and makes one tray piece and its home slot glow. PICTURE, while held, turns navy and shows the whole picture over the tray. While pictures load, the guide and the tray shimmer and play can start.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ZpLdr",
          "name": "Head · Reward",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Reward",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ITCsG",
          "name": "Body · Reward",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The last piece turns the counter green, a sparkle sweeps the picture once and the board glows. The result reveals the finished picture with WELL DONE! and a round star every time, the dinosaur's large name and one fact. FIRST BEST! or NEW BEST! with confetti appears only when that level's collection grows; the level chip shows its count out of 3, and the bar shows the shared collection. A replay is quiet. When progress can't be read, the counts and best wording are hidden, and the star and the reveal still celebrate.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sNhLC",
          "name": "Head · Motion",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Motion",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "B7r6z",
          "name": "Body · Motion",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The board, tray pages, the snap, the glide back, the sparkle sweep and the reveal use the shared motion tokens, quick rather than long; with reduced motion they become short fades.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
