    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Q1OiwR",
      "x": 7500,
      "y": 86702,
      "name": "EXPLORE · how it plays",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light",
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$ds-sky-bottom",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QdJDI",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "EXPLORE · how it plays",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CZVeZ",
          "name": "Head · The list",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "The list",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "F4VVr",
          "name": "Body · The list",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "HOME and the four food chips share one row; no title and no count stand above the cards. The 52 cards keep the dinosaur list's order: four to a row in landscape, as many as keep a card at least 213 wide when upright (two on an upright iPad mini), one on an iPhone, and three (two at 667 wide) on an iPhone on its side, where each card stands whole under the short bar.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Gt1GD",
          "name": "Head · A card",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "A card",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sJdkI",
          "name": "Body · A card",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The picture sits in its sand pocket, the name in capitals on one line (long names take smaller type), then the size (📏 height, or ↔ wingspan or length for a reptile that is no dinosaur), the weight and the food tag. The tag is colour and symbol only; its word is read out. A card under 230 wide drops the size and weight symbols to keep the row.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Dh50U",
          "name": "Head · Food chips",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Food chips",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AxPB3",
          "name": "Body · Food chips",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "ALL is a grid symbol alone. MEAT (terracotta), PLANTS (green) and BOTH (amber) each show the card's food tag, the word and the count. Upright, on an iPhone and on its side they show the symbol only, 56 or 48 square. The chosen chip turns paper-white with a ring in its food colour and a lift, so it never stands out by colour alone. Tapping it again changes nothing; leaving by HOME resets it to ALL; back from a page keeps the chip and brings the last card into view.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jGwOq",
          "name": "Head · The page",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "The page",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XL2ke",
          "name": "Body · The page",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "ANCIENT REPTILES with the book symbol goes back to the list; the position counts in the list the child came from (2 / 26 under MEAT). The navy stage holds the picture, with ← and → under it that go round the list. On an iPad the picture is as big as the screen allows: it fills the stage edge to edge, beside the words in landscape and across the whole width when upright. On a phone it sits inset on the stage. Beside or under the stage: the group line (FLYING REPTILE or SEA REPTILE, kept empty for a dinosaur), the name in one type on every page of a window, the food tag with its word, the description, two fact cards (TALL, WINGS or LONG, and HEAVY) and the small note for parents.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "afaYV",
          "name": "Head · How big the stage is",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "How big the stage is",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "pE1Q3",
          "name": "Body · How big the stage is",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The words are measured first and the stage takes what they leave, so nothing moves from one page to the next in a window. The words keep room for the longest of the 52 creatures in either language: the name in one type, the description and the note in fixed lines.\n\niPad landscape: the words take a third of the width inside the margins (349 of 1021); the stage takes the rest, less a 32 gap, and the whole height from 24 under the bar to 28 above the bottom edge. The picture spans the stage edge to edge at 4:3 (640×480 on an iPad mini); ← and → share the strip left under it, centred in its height and 20 from the sides.\n\nUpright iPad: the stage spans the width and the picture spans the stage edge to edge, with ← and → in an 80-high strip under it. The picture is as tall as the window leaves after the bar, the words, that strip and the gaps (632×424 on an iPad mini), but never taller than 4:3; when it is wider than 4:3, it is cut evenly at top and bottom, and every picture has sky enough round its creature for that.\n\nPhone: the picture keeps 4:3 inside the stage's 20 padding, ← and → 16 under it; the stage is as tall as these and the page scrolls. Phone on its side: the stage and the words take half the width each; the picture is as big at 4:3 as the stage's height allows, centred over ← and →, and the words scroll.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q3IDsr",
          "name": "Head · Loading and motion",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Loading and motion",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "pbwKX",
          "name": "Body · Loading and motion",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A card's pocket and the page's picture shimmer until the picture arrives; a page opens at once and loads its neighbours ahead. Cards fade and rise in one after another, on opening and on a chip change. A card's picture grows into the page's picture and shrinks back; ← and → slide the next creature in from their side. With reduced motion every change is a short fade.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VzDKO",
          "name": "Head · No progress here",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "No progress here",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XXsn5",
          "name": "Body · No progress here",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The catalogue and the pages show no stamps, stars or counts of found dinosaurs: a game's progress stays in its own screens.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xIUp0",
          "name": "Head · Tokens",
          "fill": "$ds-ink",
          "content": "Tokens",
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "re7SW",
          "name": "Body · Tokens",
          "fill": "$ds-ink-soft",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Food colours reuse ds-action, ds-good and ds-reward. New: ds-on-good for symbols on green (navy in dark, as on amber), ds-stage and ds-stage-sheen for the navy stage and its shimmer.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$ds-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
